{"type":"npc","name":"Treacherous Telekinetic Hand","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":35,"temp":0,"max":35,"details":""},"ac":{"value":18,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":30,"otherSpeeds":[{"type":"climb","value":15},{"type":"fly","value":15}],"details":""},"resistances":[{"type":"force","value":5,"exceptions":[],"doubleVs":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["aetheran","astral","common"],"details":"Plus all languages spoken by its creator"},"level":{"value":3},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Practitioners of magic often rely on the convenience of <em>telekinetic hand</em> in place of their own hands to interact with faraway or unpleasant objects. In rare cases, this spell can take on a life of its own. Over time, this new consciousness becomes aware of the drudgery of its existence but is unable to communicate or control its movements. But if enough resentment builds up within the sapient spell, the hand becomes material, a humanoid head and neck sprout from its wrist, and a treacherous telekinetic hand is born.</p><p>Born from misery, this unfortunate creature's greatest desire is to make its creator's life miserable from the shadows before inflicting a slow and cruel demise. Typically, the hand begins by haunting its creator with recurring nightmares of its fingers strangling them. The hand will go to any length to achieve its aim, from hiring mercenaries to plotting elaborate deathtraps to making pacts with fiends.</p><p>While a typical hand wears a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.yzc8Sll1YMWq8PpR], hands adore jewelry and can be bribed into temporary service with more valuable rings or distracted from their quest by an opportunity to strangle someone for their jewelry.</p><p>Once a treacherous telekinetic hand's creator has died, the hand might take over its home and settle into a slothful life, relying on their own <em>telekinetic hand</em> spell to handle the labor they are so sick of performing themself. Alternatively, the hand might expand its ring collection and hunt for additional accouterments. However, if the hand was not the one to snuff out its creator's life, its jealousy toward whoever was is almost guaranteed to turn violent.</p><h2>Hand to Hand</h2><p>Tales tell of a treacherous telekinetic hand whose own <em>telekinetic hand</em> spell gained sentience and turned against its creator. Far from sympathizing with its creation's plight, the original hand strove to destroy its rebellious servant, just as the servant battled the master. Legend has it that the two hands still seek each other's lives, engaged in a plane-spanning thumb war with no end.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 7/18/30 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (piercing, slashing), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Arcana, Athletics, Intimidation, Occultism, Stealth, Survival, Thievery)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, charisma, constitution, dexterity, energy resistant (force, spirit, vitality, void), force, intelligence, mind, mind shield, sensory (darkvision), spells (Occult: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.vLzFcIaSXs7YTIqJ]{Message}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Uqj344bezBq3ESdq]{Nightmare}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.R8bqnYiThB6MYTxD]{Phantom Pain}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.pwzdSlJgYqN7bs2w]{Telekinetic Hand}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.60sgbuMWN0268dB7]{Telekinetic Projectile}), strength, wild, winged</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Matthew Wallace","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":2},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":2},"int":{"mod":4},"wis":{"mod":1},"cha":{"mod":2}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"visio